* Table of the first 500 primes — Knuth TAOCP Vol.1, Program P (section 1.3.2)
*
* Output goes to the line printer (device 18).
* Open the Printer tab in the I/O panel to see the result.
*
* Algorithm:
*   Trial division: for each odd candidate N, test divisibility by all known
*   primes PRIME[K] up to sqrt(N).  Uses double-buffered printer output.
*
* Memory layout:
*   PRIME+1 .. PRIME+500  (addr 100..599)  — prime table
*   BUF0    .. BUF0+24    (addr 2000..2024) — output buffer 0 (24 data + 1 link)
*   BUF1    .. BUF1+24    (addr 2025..2049) — output buffer 1
*   3000..                                  — program

L       EQU     500
PRINTER EQU     18
PRIME   EQU     99
BUF0    EQU     2000
BUF1    EQU     BUF0+25

        ORIG    3000
START   IOC     0(PRINTER)    * skip to top of page
        LD1     =1-L=         * rI1 = 1-500 = -499
        LD2     =3=           * rI2 = 3  (first candidate N)

* ── Find primes ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2H      INC1    1             * J++
        ST2     PRIME+L,1     * PRIME[J] = N  (index: L+J = 500+J)
        J1Z     2F            * J=0 means all 500 found → jump to output

4H      INC2    2             * N += 2 (next odd candidate)
        ENT3    2             * K = 2 (start testing from PRIME[2])

6H      ENTA    0             * clear rA
        ENTX    0,2           * rX = N
        DIV     PRIME,3       * rA = N / PRIME[K],  rX = N mod PRIME[K]
        JXZ     4B            * remainder = 0 → N is composite, try next N
        CMPA    PRIME,3       * compare quotient with PRIME[K]
        INC3    1             * K++
        JG      6B            * quotient > PRIME[K] → keep testing
        JMP     2B            * quotient ≤ PRIME[K] → N is prime

* ── Print results ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
* Layout: 10 lines × 50 primes, 10 primes per line, 4 chars each.
* The inner loop fills one printer line working backwards through the prime
* table (steps of 50), so each line comes out in ascending order.

2H      OUT     TITLE(PRINTER) * print title line "FIRST FIVE HUNDRED PRIMES"
        ENT4    BUF1+10       * rI4 = buffer write pointer (starts at BUF1+10)
        ENT5    -50           * rI5 column counter

2H      INC5    L+1           * rI5 += 501  (column 451, 452, … on each outer pass)
4H      LDA     PRIME,5       * load PRIME[rI5]
        CHAR                  * convert integer → decimal digits in rA:rX
        STX     0,4(1:4)      * store 4 digits into buffer word at rI4
        DEC4    1             * buffer pointer--
        DEC5    50            * step back 50 rows in prime table
        J5P     4B            * rI5 > 0 → more primes for this line
        OUT     0,4(PRINTER)  * print 24-word line (from rI4)
        LD4     24,4          * switch buffer: follow link word at offset 24
        J5N     2B            * rI5 < 0 → more lines to print
        HLT

* ── Static data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
        ORIG    PRIME+1
        CON     2             * PRIME[1] = 2 (seed the table)

        ORIG    BUF0-5
TITLE   ALF     "FIRST"
        ALF     " FIVE"
        ALF     " HUND"
        ALF     "RED P"
        ALF     "RIMES"

        ORIG    BUF0+24
        CON     BUF1+10       * BUF0 link → BUF1

        ORIG    BUF1+24
        CON     BUF0+10       * BUF1 link → BUF0

        END     START
